  "title": "Days of the week",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Every day ends in **-বার** (*-bar*, 'day of the week'), and like English the names come from the sun, moon and planets:\n\n**রবিবার** Sun-day · **সোমবার** Moon-day · **মঙ্গলবার** (Mars) · **বুধবার** (Mercury) · **বৃহস্পতিবার** (Jupiter) · **শুক্রবার** (Venus) · **শনিবার** (Saturn)\n\n**আজ কী বার?** = 'What day is it today?'\n\n**কাল** (*kal*) means **both 'yesterday' and 'tomorrow'** — the verb's tense tells you which. With no verb, as in **কাল শনিবার**, people understand 'tomorrow'. To be explicit, say **গতকাল** (yesterday) or **আগামীকাল** (tomorrow); you'll use গতকাল in Unit 9.\n\nCulture: in Bangladesh the weekend is **Friday and Saturday**. Friday is the day of **Jumma** prayers, and Thursday night is the big night out — perfect for biryani.",
